---
import StarlightPage from '@astrojs/starlight/components/StarlightPage.astro';
---

<StarlightPage frontmatter={{ title: 'Privacy Policy', template: 'splash', hero: { tagline: '' } }}>
  <div class="legal-page" data-testid="privacy-page">
    <header class="legal-header">
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="legal-meta">Effective date: October 15, 2026 · ioTACTICAL Limited Liability Company (LLC), operating RTMX Sync and related services (the open-source RTMX CLI and hosted Sync; “RTMX”, “we”, “us”)</p>
    </header>

    <section class="legal-section">
      <h2>1. Scope</h2>
      <p>
        This policy covers rtmx.ai, managed Sync (<code>sync.rtmx.ai</code>), billing and
        checkout flows, command-line interface (CLI) login against the managed host, and related
        support channels. Self-managed or air-gapped deployments you operate are governed by your
        own policies; we do not process that customer data unless you send it to us for support.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="legal-section">
      <h2>2. Information we collect</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Account identity.</strong> Email, display name, and provider id from Open
          Authorization (OAuth) identity providers (IdPs) you choose (e.g. GitHub, Google,
          Microsoft Entra).</li>
        <li><strong>Organization and billing.</strong> Organization names, membership roles, Stripe
          customer/subscription identifiers, and entitlement state. We do not store full card
          numbers; Stripe processes payments.</li>
        <li><strong>Usage and diagnostics.</strong> Application Programming Interface (API) and
          WebSocket metadata (timestamps, organization/room identifiers, error codes), login and
          key events needed for security and abuse prevention.</li>
        <li><strong>Website.</strong> Standard server logs, optional newsletter email if you
          subscribe, and Google reCAPTCHA (automated challenge–response) tokens on form submits.</li>
        <li><strong>Sync content.</strong> Requirements and collaboration data you place in
          managed Sync rooms. Treat that data as confidential to your organization.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="legal-section">
      <h2>3. How we use information</h2>
      <p>We use data to provide and secure the service, authenticate you, bill for paid tiers,
        prevent abuse, improve reliability, and communicate service-related notices. We do not
        sell personal information.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="legal-section">
      <h2>4. Sharing</h2>
      <p>We share data with processors that help run the product (for example cloud hosting,
        Stripe for payments, and identity providers during OAuth). We may disclose information
        if required by law or to protect the service and users from fraud or security threats.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="legal-section">
      <h2>5. Retention</h2>
      <p>Account and organization records are retained while your account is active and for a
        reasonable period afterward for billing, audit, and legal obligations. You may request
        deletion of account data subject to retention required for security or compliance.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="legal-section">
      <h2>6. Security</h2>
      <p>We use industry-standard controls appropriate to a managed Software as a Service (SaaS)
        control plane (Transport Layer Security (TLS), access controls, secret management). No
        method of transmission or storage is perfectly secure; report issues to
        <a href="mailto:security@rtmx.ai">security@rtmx.ai</a>.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="legal-section">
      <h2>7. Your choices</h2>
      <p>You can disconnect OAuth by signing out and revoking the RTMX app in your IdP.
        Newsletter unsubscribe is available on those emails. Contact
        <a href="mailto:privacy@rtmx.ai">privacy@rtmx.ai</a> for access or deletion requests.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="legal-section">
      <h2>8. Children</h2>
      <p>The service is not directed to children under 16. We do not knowingly collect their
        personal information.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="legal-section">
      <h2>9. Changes</h2>
      <p>We may update this policy; the effective date above will change. Material changes will
        be noted on this page.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="legal-section">
      <h2>10. Contact</h2>
      <p>
        ioTACTICAL LLC<br />
        Privacy: <a href="mailto:privacy@rtmx.ai">privacy@rtmx.ai</a><br />
        General: <a href="/contact">Contact</a>
      </p>
      <p class="legal-related">Also see our <a href="/terms">Terms of Service</a>.</p>
    </section>
  </div>
</StarlightPage>

<style is:global>
  .legal-page { max-width: 42rem; margin: 0 auto; padding: 1.5rem 1.25rem 3rem; color: var(--rtmx-text); }
  .legal-header { text-align: center; margin-bottom: 2rem; }
  .legal-header h1 {
    font-size: 2.25rem; font-weight: 700; margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--rtmx-emerald) 0%, var(--rtmx-emerald-light) 100%);
    -webkit-background-clip: text; -webkit-text-fill-color: transparent; background-clip: text;
  }
  .legal-meta { color: var(--rtmx-text-muted); font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 1.5; }
  .legal-section { margin-bottom: 1.75rem; }
  .legal-section h2 { font-size: 1.15rem; color: var(--rtmx-emerald-light); margin: 0 0 0.5rem; }
  .legal-section p, .legal-section li { color: var(--rtmx-text-muted); line-height: 1.65; }
  .legal-section ul { padding-left: 1.25rem; margin: 0.5rem 0 0; }
  .legal-section li { margin-bottom: 0.4rem; }
  .legal-related { margin-top: 1rem; }
</style>
